# item98j: Kello01a by player input, from PlayerStart to `Find the chalet` and the Kello01b travel.
# Self-contained (the shared kello01a_route.script is not used by this route). Input only:
# `goto`/`jump` waypoints, `select_weapon`/`track`/`fire`/`reload` for the authored soldier fights.
# No teleport, weapon grant, item, set_goal or control override.
#
# Start: MapInfo `Kello0` (XIDMaps.Kello01), one objective `[0 P] Find the chalet`, PlayerStart0
# (-3005.8, 6127.0, 90.6) UU, health 150, map-entry loadout (magnum group 3 with 12 rounds, FusilPompe
# group 9 and FusilChasse group 10 sharing 13 shells; no MedKit, no armour).
#
# Sections (script seconds; a fight stalls the waypoint chain, which is position based):
#   1.0-28.9      walk the item98e valley loop to the start bowl (same lines as kello01a_route.script)
#   29.0-29.5     bowl shotgunners: BaseSoldier9 (1 magnum round), BaseSoldier0 (2 rounds)
#   29.5-74.1     waypoint chain down the valley without the 38-HP bank fall of the old route
#   74.1-75.6     first strike on the three-soldier ambush from the rim: BaseSoldier (1 round),
#                 BaseSoldier2 (1), BaseSoldier1 (2)
#   75.6-98       lake ice: short `goto` hops, jumping the open-water channels between the floes
#   99.4-128      far shore: BaseSoldier4 (2 rounds at ~3200 UU), BaseSoldier8 (1), BaseSoldier3 (2);
#                 that is the 12th and last magnum round
#   128-206       west cliffs and the chalet approach: NoControl cutscene 142.5-155.0 (input is
#                 ignored there), then BaseSoldier12/10/13/11/15 with the FusilChasse/FusilPompe
#                 (select_weapon 10/9, shells shared), chain to the chalet porch (-18923,4787)
#   ~209.15       Trigger0 -> XIIIGoalTrigger0 completes `Find the chalet`; the map's own DoTravel
#                 requests Kello01b.unr
# The waypoint chain (each `goto x y` and its optional `jump`) was generated offline by a best-first
# search over the real PlayerSim (same walker and water volumes; hops that touch a water volume or
# land harder than the retail fall-damage threshold are rejected). The weapon selections and reloads
# are the recorded authoring-time aim assist; item107e replaced its `track`/`fire` volleys with
# named standing engagements (`engage_on <Actor>`), so each pinned soldier is aimed at by name and
# tapped at the measured cadence while the waypoint clock keeps running.
t=1.0 select_weapon 3
